  "published": "2026-11-09T10:28:34.907Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.1: Pull points are released, not abandoned. EventService1 gains DisposeAsync (Dispose does the same for synchronous callers): it stops the receive loop, waits for it, unsubscribes over the still-open subscription manager with a bounded deadline, and only then closes the clients. The old order closed the clients under the loop, so its Unsubscribe was lost and the camera kept the pull point — a camera with a small MaxPullPoints ran out after a series of restarts and then refused every new subscription. Re-subscribing now releases the old pull point first on both paths, including after a fault, so a camera at its cap frees a slot instead of losing the subscription for good. StopReceivingAsync now stops deterministically, and a refused CreatePullPointSubscription logs the camera's advertised MaxPullPoints. 1.3.0: Geolocation on Camera — GetGeoLocationAsync and SetGeoLocationAsync, with the ONVIF *Specified flags honoured so a coordinate the camera did not report is absent rather than zero. Device I/O live state: DeviceIoStateWatcher opens a topic-filtered pull point on Device/Trigger/Relay and Device/Trigger/DigitalInput, where the Initialized snapshot gives each relay's and input's current state and Changed gives every update, and keeps it as a TryGetState snapshot with a change event. DeviceIoState carries a relay's logical state and contact. The probe gains geolocation steps and shows live relay and input state. New unit tests project (not packaged).",
